(LANGUAGE.md, "Type Immutability": `roster is <value>.`, `the roster is
 <value>.` and `Set roster to <value>.` all write a name that is already
 declared, and all three are checked the same way. The function reading the
 global reads whichever spelling wrote it last.)

a list called roster is [].

To 'how many'.
    Return a number, roster's length.

Set roster to ["ada"].
Print 'how many'.

the roster is ["ada", "grace"].
Print 'how many'.

roster is ["ada", "grace", "katherine"].
Print 'how many'.
